   "text": "The phone stand is built in the project as \"Phone stand\", 80 x 45.2 x 58 mm. It passes the plan check (closed body, minimum wall 2 mm). I haven't sliced or sent it to the printer.\n\n- **Shape:** the phone sits back at 60 degrees from the desk, held by a 6 mm rear support and a base 6 mm thick. The 10 mm front lip is angled about 17 degrees toward the phone so it stays put.\n- **Cable gap:** 12 mm wide, centered on the lip, cut down to the base top. The floor dips 0.5 mm into the base to avoid a zero-thickness sliver.\n- **Sizes I guessed:** the 12 mm cable gap, the 4 mm lip thickness, the 6 mm support thickness and the 60 mm phone contact length on the support. These are on the dimension sheet you confirmed, so tell me if your phone or cable needs something different.\n- **Printing:** it lies flat on the bed, and the steepest overhang is about 30 degrees from vertical, so I expect no supports are needed.\n\nNext step: I can slice it for the P1S in PLA at 0.4 mm and, if you want it printed, send it once you approve."
